n be silently broken.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5899a1dfcc8b6ee6","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria — 'A truncated run cannot be silent' / 'The truncation signal needs no network call'","norm_id":"n6b79891835688481","priority":0.7556,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Completion signal added after mirror_out_of_sync, or reserve-clamp reorders publishes, breaking the existing nine-alarm dead-man"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State a concrete default for PROBE_TAIL_RESERVE_SEC (e.g. seconds needed for the counter/completion-signal publish path) and derive the stated clamped-portion bound and margin from it.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5d","T5e"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2137,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'define budget_left = PROBE_DEADLINE_SEC - elapsed - PROBE_TAIL_RESERVE_SEC'","'bounded by construction at PROBE_DEADLINE_SEC - PROBE_TAIL_RESERVE_SEC. State that bound and the margin it leaves.'","No numeric default is given for PROBE_TAIL_RESERVE_SEC while PROBE_DEADLINE_SEC is pinned to TimeoutStartSec (240s)"],"finding":"PROBE_TAIL_RESERVE_SEC is referenced in the grant formula and the 'clamped portion' bound but is never assigned a concrete value or default, so the derived bound (PROBE_DEADLINE_SEC - PROBE_TAIL_RESERVE_SEC) and 'the margin it leaves' cannot be evaluated as written.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffc24041b2d8dafc5","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria — deadline/reserve bullets","norm_id":"n2457b3a8bc832cac","priority":0.5863,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor must pick a reserve value to make the tail-publish criterion pass and cannot know how much margin the author intends"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Fix a default such as PROBE_TAIL_RESERVE_SEC=20 sized to cover the tail publish + completion-signal write, giving a clamped bound of 220s inside the 240s timeout and a stated ~20s margin.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the truncation signal's transport and reconcile 'needs no network call' with 'must feed CloudWatch dead-man alarms' (e.g. a network-free local marker consumed later, plus a separate published heartbeat), so the signal can fire during a network/CloudWatch stall.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.398,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["observability.sh:1511/1462 publish via `aws cloudwatch put-metric-data` (a network call)","plan: 'The truncation signal needs no network call, so it publishes during the stall it reports'","the dead-man alarms it must feed are CloudWatch alarms, which require the signal to reach CloudWatch"],"finding":"The AC 'The truncation signal needs no network call, so it publishes during the stall it reports' is in tension with the plan's own consequence model, in which 'a metric's POSITION decides whether it survives' and every published signal is a CloudWatch put-metric-data — which IS a network call. A CloudWatch metric cannot both be network-free and serve as the truncation signal; the signal's transport (local journald/logger breadcrumb vs. a published metric vs. a filesystem marker) is left unspecified, and the mechanism differs materially by choice.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5b4f3838b51d7e1f","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria — 'The truncation signal needs no network call, so it publishes during the stall it reports'","norm_id":"n98dbdb1c0676a002","priority":0.402,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A network/CloudWatch stall is the very condition being reported; if the signal is a put-metric-data it cannot get out, defeating the AC","If the signal is only a local journald breadcrumb, no CloudWatch alarm can observe it"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Quantify the completion criterion: define the induced-I/O load level (matching the observed clustering) and a specific consecutive-run count (e.g. N clean runs) required to close it.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5d","T5e"],"criteria":["E2","F1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4071,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'under representative load over consecutive runs' — no run count or load definition","Contrast with the precise defect-seeded criterion that drives a specific call past budget"],"finding":"The completion criterion 'completes within its timeout under representative load over consecutive runs' leaves 'representative load' and the number of 'consecutive runs' unquantified, unlike the deterministic defect-seeded criterion.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb884be76af1f5bf0","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria — 'The probe completes within its timeout under representative load over consecutive runs.'","norm_id":"nbe4f3628d4635cf9","priority":0.3929,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer cannot decide how many clean consecutive runs, or what induced I/O level, closes this criterion"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State e.g. 'zero timeout kills across 20 consecutive runs while a background du/fio load reproduces the 1.88M-file walk contention.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7143,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Qualify 'every expensive call is timeout-wrapped / no unbounded blocker' to note that calls route through the `bounded()` helper (observability.sh:395-397), which degrades to an UNBOUNDED direct exec when the `timeout` binary is absent, and correct 'literal timeout 15 on ... git ls-remote' (ls-remote is `bounded 15` at line 1499).","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4089,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Every expensive call is ALREADY `timeout`-wrapped ... literal `timeout 15` on the docker/`git ls-remote` calls. There is no unbounded blocker to find.'","observability.sh:1499 `github_sha=$(bounded 15 git ls-remote ...)` — bounded, not literal timeout","observability.sh:395-397: `bounded() { timeout \"$@\"; }` only when `command -v timeout` succeeds; else `bounded() { shift; \"$@\"; }` runs unbounded","observability.sh:388 comment: `timeout` is coreutils and present on the deployment host, but not on every host this script is exercised on — so the no-unbounded-blocker premise holds only where timeout exists"],"finding":"The premise 'every expensive call is ALREADY timeout-wrapped ... there is no unbounded blocker to find' is slightly overstated: git ls-remote uses the bounded helper (not a literal 'timeout 15'), and bounded() degrades to running the command with NO wall-clock bound when the timeout binary is absent (observability.sh:388-397). The 'literal timeout 15 on the docker/git ls-remote calls' wording is also imprecise — only docker ps/stats (1084/1087) are literal timeout; ls-remote is bounded 15 (1499).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa25eff198a8fb776","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'The mechanism is CUMULATIVE, not a single unbounded call'","norm_id":"n2cdc66c9f875d1a4","priority":0.3911,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A validation/CI host without coreutils `timeout` exercises the probe; bounded calls run unbounded, so the 'no unbounded blocker' framing does not hold there","A reader takes 'every expensive call is timeout-wrapped' as literal and is surprised the grant-helper AC (which the plan itself requires) must also cover the timeout-absent degradation path"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reword to: 'Every expensive call is bounded via the `bounded()` helper (a `timeout` wrapper that degrades to unbounded direct exec when the timeout binary is missing) or a literal `timeout N` (docker ps/stats).' State that the deployment host has coreutils `timeout`, so the diagnosis holds there, and confirm the grant helper also covers the timeout-absent branch.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"3461692cbc1ce75f","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["ffee57386511a9f1",7994],"description_boxes":["a453c4f4c4b8f0c2",0],"file_impact":["0c04b9bc43ae8006",5],"ticket_id":["f33d35f2fceb40c6",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":391860,"cache_write_tokens":149186,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":11726.3,"input_tokens":563227,"llm_calls":31,"llm_ms":236168.6,"output_tokens":22090,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":282071.1,"verify_requests":10},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","priority_floor":0.8,"provider_provenance":{"candidates":["bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6"],"capabilities":{"native_structured_output":true,"prompt_cache_style":"bedrock","supports_temperature":true,"supports_thinking":true,"web_access":"off"},"endpoint_host":nul